{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmsDhwZM5vcMeQRWH4b6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The verdict is MEANING for all four rows (SR-229, LLR-300, TC-316, TC-318), and I re-anchored all four.**\n\nThe amendment gives the holder a new action: it can hand its own lease back. Before, the text said a latched drain ends *only* when the owner clears it, the owner releases it, or a relaunched successor takes the lease. That list was complete, so an implementation letting the holder free its own lease broke the old text. Under the new text, an implementation without that path fails.\n\n- **SR-229:** both the Requirement and AcceptanceCriteria cells changed meaning. They add the hand-back as a fourth way the drain ends, plus new refusals:\n  - a caller other than the holder is refused;\n  - a handoff with no session prompt is refused;\n  - the holder's own pending relaunch request blocks the hand-back.\n\n  They also add two new conditions: with the guard off, the hand-back touches nothing, and a previous holder's leftover request does not block it.\n- **LLR-300:** the Detail cell adds a `hand_back` operation with its own refusal contract, and changes the list of ways the latch can end.\n- **TC-316:** the pass condition (Expected) moved, and the Method adds new assertions. It also drops one old assertion, that only three acts end the latch, which is now false.\n- **TC-318:** the Method extends the command-line exit-code checks to the new `handback` subcommand.\n\n**Why I blessed them:** the rung is released, so re-attesting was mine to do. The new text matches WI-842's Done-when. `hand_back` in `project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py:773` does the refusals in the order the text states and returns early with the guard off. `python -m pytest -q tests/test_coordinator_guard.py` ran 77 tests and all passed. I did not edit any registry cell, and there was nothing to send back through `## Dispositions`.\n\n**Commits**, each with the `WI: WI-842` trailer and with the commit hooks passing:\n1. `f1b9a5d0` records the verdict in `docs/reviews/wi-842-coordinator-hands-back-lease/001-ADJUDICATE-b6c13a8.md`, ending `VERDICT: MEANING rows=4`.\n2. `49d9f891` is the act: `python project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py snapshot --reattests SR-229,LLR-300,TC-316,TC-318`. It is recorded as act 41, and the snapshot changed only those four rows. No other row was refused for drift. The script is at `project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py`; the instruction's `scripts/intake.py` path doesn't exist in this checkout.\n\nOne warning from the hooks for the coordinator: WI-842 is still `status=active` while commits carry its trailer. The warning says this is a prompt to reconcile, not a reason to close.\n\n**Not available here:** the Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors need authorizing in claude.ai's connector settings before they work. Nothing in this task needed them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_read_input_tokens":61828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":625},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d0f516d-2508-4163-a072-c622b5b0abf8","uuid":"af46243b-d8c4-4fc5-875e-36aa978ae5e7","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:40:17.077Z","request_id":"req_011CfmsDhH7yLUpzVHMcjHMN"}
